  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "y9DXHU6arHnmS3CxI7f1Un4ezyk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:36.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`PollBehavior` is set per remote in `RemoteOptions` and controls only the schedule, never whether the channel connects:\n\n```typescript\nenum PollBehavior { Auto = \"auto\", Manual = \"manual\" }\n```\n\n`Auto` is the default. The channel runs its interval timer in the background: **the first tick fires immediately on `init()`**, then repeats every `pollIntervalMs` (default 2000 ms). That immediate first tick matters \u2014 adding an `Auto` remote produces a fetch straight away, not after one interval.\n\n`Manual` still registers and connects the channel; it simply never ticks on its own. Pulls happen only when you ask:\n\n```typescript\ntriggerPull(name: string): void;\n```\n\n`triggerPull` runs exactly one pull cycle. For a `Manual` remote it does **not** promote it to recurring polling \u2014 the remote stays `Manual` and a single fetch runs. This makes `Manual` the right choice for test harnesses, on-demand refresh buttons, and any environment where you want deterministic control over when network traffic happens.\n\nTwo edge behaviors: `triggerPull` on an unknown remote throws ``Remote with name '${name}' does not exist``, and on a `GqlResponseChannel` (the Switchboard push side) it is a **no-op**, because that channel has nothing to poll.\n\nPolling is not a naive timer. Two mechanisms guard the reactor:\n\n- **Backpressure** \u2014 a tick *defers* when the reactor queue depth exceeds `maxQueueDepth` (default 100) and rechecks after `backpressureCheckIntervalMs` (default 500 ms). A saturated reactor stops pulling more work onto itself rather than piling it up. This is why `GqlRequestChannelFactory` needs the queue passed to its constructor.\n- **Exponential backoff** \u2014 transient poll failures retry between `retryBaseDelayMs` (default 1000) and `retryMaxDelayMs` (default 300000, i.e. five minutes).\n\nAll four are optional `parameters` on the `\"gql\"` channel config alongside the required `url`, and each is type-checked at registration: a wrong type throws, for example `'\"pollIntervalMs\" parameter must be a number'`.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/04-Synchronization.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:36.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:36.000Z"
    }
  },
